         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### ISKAY\n\nISKAY means \"two\" in Quechua. This movement applies when two circles occupy the square labeled with the number 2. One circle is shifted to the square with value 1, and the other to the square with value 3.\n\n2 + 2 = 1 + 3\n\nThis transformation is also known as the \"short open\" method because the circles move to adjacent squares.\n\nUse the green arrow to perform this movement and update the fingers. Use the blue arrow to return to the original position.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "c29e24ae-e1cc-4f2c-b7f2-c8c30496b3c8",
         "prev": "",
