               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### KIMSA\n\nKIMSA means \"three\" in Quechua. This movement applies when two circles occupy the square labeled with the number 3. One circle moves to the square labeled 1, and the other to the square labeled 5.\n\n3 + 3 = 1 + 5\n\nThis transformation is known as the \"large open\" method because the circles move to the two ends of the line.\n\nUse the green arrow to perform this movement and update the fingers. Use the blue arrow to return to the original position.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "06d78b90-63c4-4804-99da-bf95e93127df",
