                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### PISQA\n\nPISQA means \"five\" in Quechua. This movement applies when two circles are stacked in the square labeled with the number 5. One circle moves to the square labeled 1 on the top line, and the other is removed, so the stack passes to the top line.\n\n5 + 5 = 10 + 0\n\nUse the green arrow to perform this movement and update the fingers. Use the blue arrow to return to the original position.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "c4187516-c4fc-46ef-9cc4-9b24704da99f",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
