               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### PICHANA\n\nPICHANA means \"broom\" in Quechua. This movement applies when two circles sit in squares whose sum equals the value of another square, so the two values merge into one square.\n\n1 + 2 = 3 + 0\n2 + 3 = 5 + 0\n\nUse the green arrow to perform this movement and update the fingers. Use the blue arrow to return to the original position.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
